The team compares the two Resilience4j bulkhead types for the export call:

```java
@Bulkhead(name = "reports")                                   // type = SEMAPHORE (default)
Report export(Month m) { ... }

@Bulkhead(name = "reports", type = Bulkhead.Type.THREADPOOL)
CompletableFuture<Report> exportAsync(Month m) { ... }
```

Statement: "Both types run the export on a separate thread pool, so a slow export never blocks the thread of the request that started it."
